    "# Quiz: The Data Science Lifecycle: Analyzing\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-15-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Analyzing can refer to analyzing models or data</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>True</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Analyzing checks that the data can answer the questions, and it can also check a model.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>False</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Analyzing can check the data, and it can also check that a model answers the questions.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-15-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is important about exploring data before using it in a model or further analysis?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>To remove data</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Exploring is about getting to know the data and finding its challenges, not removing it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Identify challenges in the data</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Exploring helps you get to know the data and find the challenges of working with it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Exploring data isn't important</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Exploring tells you whether the data can support your goal and what its challenges are.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-15-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What are some things a data scientist will do when exploring data?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Sampling</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Sampling is one way to explore data, but so are visualizations.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Visualizations</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Visualizations are one way to explore data, but so is sampling.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>All of the above</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Sampling and visualizations are both ways to explore data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-15-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Visualization is never part of exploratory data analysis (EDA)</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>True</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Visualizing data while exploring helps you spot patterns, relationships and problems.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>False</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Visuals made while exploring help you spot patterns, relationships and problems in the data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-15-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which Panda functions provides basic data profiling?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>pandas()</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The function for descriptive statistics is describe(). It gives the count, min, max, mean and more.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>isnull()</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. isnull() checks for missing values. describe() gives a summary of the data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>describe()</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. describe() gives the count, min, max, mean, standard deviation and quantiles of numeric data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-15-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is the purpose of sampling data?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Sampling is better than data profiling when looking for errors</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Sampling's purpose is to help you understand a large dataset that takes too long to explore in full.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Sampling doesn't serve a purpose</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Sampling helps you understand what is in a dataset and draw general conclusions.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Sampling is used to analyze data in a large data set because it's hard to analyze all of it</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Exploring a whole large dataset takes a long time, so a sample helps you understand it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
